==============================================================================
(A) EXHAUSTIVE SPECTRUM, n = 3..6
==============================================================================
  n = 3 : |spectrum| = 2     max = 3    
     attained : [1, 3]
     MISSING odd values below the max : []
  n = 4 : |spectrum| = 3     max = 5    
     attained : [1, 3, 5]
     MISSING odd values below the max : []
  n = 5 : |spectrum| = 7     max = 15   
     attained : [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13, 15]
     MISSING odd values below the max : [7]
  n = 6 : |spectrum| = 19    max = 45   
     attained : [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, 19, 23, 25, 27, 29, 31, 33, 37, 41, 43, 45]
     MISSING odd values below the max : [7, 21, 35, 39]

==============================================================================
(B) NESTING (stabilisation lemma):  spectrum(n) subset spectrum(n+1) ?
==============================================================================
  spectrum(3) subset spectrum(4) : True  
  spectrum(4) subset spectrum(5) : True  
  spectrum(5) subset spectrum(6) : True  
  -> consistent with the lemma; the spectra are nested, so 'the spectrum'
     is the increasing union and the gap question is well-posed.

==============================================================================
