==============================================================================
  n = 7 : values <= 60 after sampling : [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, 19, 23, 25, 27, 29, 31, 33, 35, 37, 39, 41, 43, 45, 47, 49, 51, 53, 55, 57, 59]
  n = 8 : values <= 60 after sampling : [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, 19, 23, 25, 27, 29, 31, 33, 35, 37, 39, 41, 43, 45, 47, 49, 51, 53, 55, 57, 59]
  n = 9 : values <= 60 after sampling : [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, 19, 23, 25, 27, 29, 31, 33, 35, 37, 39, 41, 43, 45, 47, 49, 51, 53, 55, 57, 59]

==============================================================================
(E) VERDICT ON THE GAPS
==============================================================================
  union of everything found, odd values <= 60 NOT attained : [7, 21]
  7   attained anywhere in this search : False
  21  attained anywhere in this search : False

  Values missing at n = 6 but FILLED IN at larger n (so not permanent):
     [35, 39]
  Values missing at n = 6 and STILL missing: [7, 21]

  DETECTION FLOOR (MISTAKE-196): (A),(B) are exhaustive and prove
  non-attainment for n <= 6.  (C),(D) are searches -- they can only prove
  ATTAINMENT.  The flip search is exhaustive for feedback-arc-set <= 4,
  so non-attainment of 7 and 21 is established for all tournaments within
  4 flips of transitive at n <= 9, and NOT beyond that.
